      "text": "Geotechnical engineering is the discipline concerned with the engineering behavior of earth materials. Every structure sits on or in the ground. Before you can design a foundation, a slope, a retaining wall, or an underground excavation, you need to understand what the ground is made of, how it behaves under load, and how it changes over time."
